{"step_index":6946,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T13:59:05Z","thinking":"This policy aims to restrict the creation or updating of Service Account API keys, but only if the target service isn't listed in the allowed services parameter. The logic suggests a deny action if any target service isn't explicitly whitelisted.  It seems to involve an IAM constraint applied at the project level, potentially to a specific resource type. Examining `resource_types`, `method_types`, and `condition` will clarify the exact access restriction.\n\n\nThis is a Google Cloud IAM constraint named `iam.managed.disableServiceAccountApiKeyCreation` applied within the `irak-mahmud-project`. The policy disallows the creation or update of Service Account API keys unless their target services are explicitly limited to a predefined list. Currently, the only allowed service is `generativelanguage.googleapis.com`. Consequently, any attempt to create a service account key for a different service, such as Google Drive, would be blocked.\n\n\nThe constraint distinguishes between standard JSON keys and API Key bindings for service accounts. The current setup only permits the creation or update of API keys for the `generativelanguage.googleapis.com` service. The issue arises when an API key is desired for Google Drive, which is currently blocked by this constraint.\n\nTo resolve the Google Drive access restriction, either `drive.googleapis.com` must be added to the allowed services in the policy, or a standard JSON key should be used instead of an API Key binding. Alternatively, using an OAuth 2.0 client ID bypasses the API key binding restriction entirely.\n\n\nThe policy restricts API key bindings, specifically denying any service not explicitly allowed, currently only the AI API. Attempting to bind an API key to Google Drive will be blocked due to the missing `drive.googleapis.com` entry in the allowed services list.\n\nOne workaround involves creating a JSON key directly within the service account, which bypasses the API key binding restriction. Alternatively, explicitly adding `drive.googleapis.com` to the allowed service list would also permit Drive access.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c '\\nlines = [\\n    \\\"ইরাক ভাইয়া, আপনি যে পলিসিটি শেয়ার করেছেন,\\\",\\n    \\\"তার সহজ ও নিখুঁত টেকনিক্যাল ব্যাখ্যা দিচ্ছি: 🎯\\\",\\n    \\\"«──────────────────────────────»\\\",\\n    \\\"★ *১. এই পলিসির কাজ কী:*\\\",\\n    \\\"* এটি আপনার `irak-mahmud-project`-এর একটি\\\",\\n    \\\"  কড়া নিরাপত্তা পলিসি (IAM Constraint)।\\\",\\n    \\\"* এর নিয়ম: সার্ভিস একাউন্টে সাধারণ API Key\\\",\\n    \\\"  যুক্ত করা ব্লক (DENY) থাকবে,\\\",\\n    \\\"* বর্তমানে কেবল *Gemini API* অনুমোদন করা আছে:\\\",\\n    \\\"  `generativelanguage.googleapis.com`\\\",\\n    \\\"«──────────────────────────────»\\\",\\n    \\\"★ *২. ড্রাইভ ব্যাকআপে এর প্রভাব:*\\\",\\n    \\\"* ড্রাইভের জন্য API Key ব্যবহার করতে চাইলে\\\",\\n    \\\"  গুগল ক্লাউড তা আটকে দেবে, কারণ লিস্টে\\\",\\n    \\\"  `drive.googleapis.com` অনুমোদিত নেই।\\\",\\n    \\\"«──────────────────────────────»\\\",\\n    \\\"★ *৩. সমাধানের সহজ উপায়:*\\\",\\n    \\\"* *উপায় ক (পলিসি না বদলে — সবচেয়ে সহজ):*\\\",\\n    \\\"  API Key বানানোর দরকার নেই। সার্ভিস একাউন্টে ঢুকে\\\",\\n    \\\"  \\\\\\\"Keys\\\\\\\" ট্যাব থেকে সরাসরি **JSON Key** নিন\\\",\\n    \\\"  (Add Key -> Create new key -> JSON)।\\\",\\n    \\\"* *উপায় খ (পলিসিতে \n<truncated 301 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking line lengths for policy explanation\"","toolSummary":"\"Verify line lengths policy explanation\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
